#X text 18 64 [tapmatrix~ [-float|-fixed] [-oversample] <ins> <outs> <maxdelay-ms> [ramp-ms]]: one multichannel signal in (<ins> channels) \, one out (<outs> channels). Each output is the sum of its taps. 4-point interpolation as delread4~., f 104;
#X text 20 111 -float (default): 32-bit float. -fixed: 16-bit fixed point (ESP32-P4 SIMD: several times faster \; elsewhere for testing \; signals within -1..1). -oversample: the delay line read at 2x: flat up to 20 kHz \, float only \, delays from 25 samples., f 104;
#X obj 20 180 osc~ 440;
#X obj 120 180 noise~;
#X obj 120 210 *~ 0.2;
#X obj 20 245 snake~ in 2;
#X msg 300 180 tap 0 0 10 0.5 \, tap 1 1 12.5 0.3;
#X text 560 180 static taps: input 0 -> output 0 after 10 ms at gain 0.5 ..., f 30;
#X msg 300 215 tap 0 2 30 0.4 200;
#X text 560 215 move to 30 ms within 200 ms (ramp), f 30;
#X msg 300 250 tap 0 2 5 0.4 500;
#X text 560 250 ... back to 5 ms within 500 ms;
#X msg 300 285 tap 1 3 50 0.2 \, tap 0 3 0 0;
#X text 560 285 gain 0: the tap is silent \; 0 ms means 1 sample, f 30;
#X msg 300 320 ramp 50;
#X text 560 320 default ramp time for later tap messages, f 30;
#X msg 300 355 clear;
#X text 560 355 all gains to 0 at once, f 30;
#X msg 300 390 engine float;
#X text 560 390 switch the engine while running, f 30;
#X msg 300 414 engine fixed;
#X obj 20 480 tapmatrix~ 2 4 100;
#X obj 30 519 snake~ out 4;
