#X text 31 640 Diagnostics (right outlet):;
#X msg 20 670 check 750;
#X text 120 670 accuracy test \, fixed only: for the next 750 blocks (1 s) the object also computes everything in float and compares. Then it sends "check <SNR> <peak error>": signal-to-error ratio of fixed against float in dB \, and the largest difference. Costs as much again while it runs., f 80;
#X msg 20 750 stats 300;
#X text 120 750 time measurement: averaged over the next 300 blocks \, per 64-sample block: how many moving taps were computed in fixed and in float \, then microseconds for the whole object and for its parts (writing the inputs into the delay lines \, preparing the moving taps \, the moving-tap and the static-tap computation)., f 80;
